WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.240
Before you see him soar into action, here's
a look back at some of the other works you

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.370
may have seen Zachary Levi star in.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:09.580
If you were wondering, this is why the actor
playing Shazam looks so familiar.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.540
For his first-ever film gig, Levi nabbed a
supporting role in the TV movie Big Shot:

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.720
Confessions of a Campus Bookie.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:22.380
The film aired on FX in March of 2002, and
although the movie was a dud, it was a great

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.500
opportunity for Levi to add a film credit
to his acting resume.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.000
Prior to Big Shot, he had only performed in
theater productions.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.590
With Big Shot, Levi was able to get his feet
wet in Hollywood, which potentially acted

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.140
as a springboard for his career's next big
achievement.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:43.111
ABC's Less Than Perfect was a moderately successful
workplace sitcom that debuted in 2002 and

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.560
ran through 2006.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.300
The show followed Sara Rue's Claude Casey,
an employee at a television network.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:53.900
Other big names in the cast included Sherri
Shepherd and Andy Dick, who played Claude's

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:54.580
coworkers.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.620
However, it was Levi who truly made a name
for himself as Kipp Steadman, Claude's elitist

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:01.000
frenemy and primary rival.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.040
He appeared in all 81 episodes of the series.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.560
"We're gonna pretend like you guys didn't
do this on purpose."

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.140
"Can we at least give it a shot?"

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.760
Playing Kipp, Levi started to see his life
change.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:19.100
In a 2003 interview with Relevant Magazine,
the then-22-year-old opened up about his newfound

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:19.640
fame:

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.080
"It's weird.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.200
To me, it hasn't all completely sunk in yet.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.740
But at the same time, I hope it never does…

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.660
I hope there's always at least a small part
of me that's always surprised, always taken

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.100
aback, always childlike or innocent in the
whole process."

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:38.380
Considering that in Shazam! he played a 14-year-old
in an adult's body, Levi apparently got his

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:38.920
wish.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:46.000
2006's Big Momma's House 2 starred Martin
Lawrence reprising his role of FBI agent Malcolm

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.420
Turner and his undercover alter ego "Big Momma."

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:53.320
Although its premise is very similar to the
first film, the sequel does inject a few new

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.520
faces to its story.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.400
One of those new additions is Zachary Levi,
who plays an FBI agent.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.200
Although Big Momma's House 2 failed to live
up to its predecessor in terms of both revenue

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.959
and reviews, it was actually a huge milestone
for Levi's career, marking the first time

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.120
his presence would grace the big screen in
theaters.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.940
You can safely assume that being on the set
of a film with a production budget of $40

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:18.640
million was at least slightly different from
Levi's sitcom experience.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:25.560
In his breakthrough role on NBC's cult favorite
TV series Chuck, Levi played Chuck Bartowski,

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.060
computer-geek-turned-secret-agent.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:32.500
The show perfectly showcased Levi's full arsenal
of acting chops, from humorously innocent

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.800
to surprisingly badass.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.940
"C-Casey?"

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:44.060
His chemistry with Yvonne Strahovski, who
portrayed Chuck's CIA handler Sarah Walker,

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.520
also proved that he could convincingly maintain
a love interest on-screen.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:51.080
Chuck was a major part of Levi's life, and
it isn't a role he’ll soon to forget.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.660
Speaking with Entertainment Weekly, Levi didn't
hide his desire to make a Chuck full-length

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:56.180
feature film:

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.760
"I'd love to do it.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.280
As far as I know, I'm the only person who's
affiliated with the show that's been trying

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.800
to make it happen on some level.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.980
I've had meetings with various people.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:06.800
There's just so many moving parts."

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:12.250
If Levi's career continues to blossom, don't
be surprised to see Chuck: The Movie eventually

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:12.780
hit theaters.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:18.560
After the first season of Chuck, Levi starred
in the road trip comedy Wieners.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.730
In the film, Levi, Keenan Thompson, and Fran
Kranz play three friends who embark on a cross-country

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.440
mission to hunt down a talk-show host who's
wronged one of them.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.640
Oh, and they drive a hot dog-shaped vehicle
to get there.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.180
Obviously.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:36.650
Unsurprisingly, Wieners failed to impress
audiences and was possibly a low point for

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.600
Levi's budding career.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:42.200
However, he had to know that the movie wasn't
exactly going to be up for any awards from

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:42.720
the start.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.620
The hot dog car was probably the first of
several clues.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:51.460
2008's Shades of Ray is difficult to assign
a specific genre.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.740
With layers of comedy, drama and romance,
it's sort of a cinematic hodgepodge.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:00.160
The indie film tells the story of Ray, whose
parents are of different ethnic backgrounds,

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.020
and his quest to find the right woman.

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:07.000
In the movie, Levi starred in the title role
as Ray, marking his first film appearance

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:07.900
as the main protagonist.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:12.880
Although Shades of Ray wasn't a box office
hit, it did well on the festival circuit,

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.120
winning various awards.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:21.180
Sure, it's cool to be able to say you've starred
in projects alongside Hollywood legends like

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.520
Clint Eastwood, Tom Hanks, or Meryl Streep,
but only a very select few have the super-cool

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.880
privilege of saying they've starred alongside
Alvin and the Chipmunks.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:33.539
In 2009's Alvin and the Chipmunks: The Squeakquel,
Levi played Toby, the video game-obsessed

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.980
cousin of Jason Lee's Chipmunk-daddy Dave.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:42.260
The kids movie was a major box office hit,
raking in over $443 million worldwide and

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.980
becoming the ninth top-grossing movie of the
year.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:46.780
Good job, Levi!

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.560
"Oh man!

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:52.380
It burns!"

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:00.780
In RocketJump Studios' web series Video Game
High School, video gaming has become the most

00:05:00.789 --> 00:05:05.309
popular sport in the future, and VGH is an
organization that teaches a wide curriculum

00:05:05.309 --> 00:05:06.580
of various gaming genres.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:11.080
The series has built up a cult following since
it kicked off in 2012.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:17.000
Although he only appeared in three episodes,
Levi's time on VGHS left a lasting impression.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:21.520
His Texas drawl and deadpan attitude makes
the introduction to his first-person shooter

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.980
course arguably one of the best scenes in
the show's first season.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:28.100
"Hello students, and welcome to FPS 101.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:33.120
My name is Ace, you can call me Ace.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:33.640
Sound good?

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.160
Fantastic."

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.800
Zachary Levi made comic book movie headlines
in 2012 when it was announced that he would

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.680
replace Josh Dallas as Fandral in Thor: The
Dark World.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:47.960
Although it was a minor role in a film that
already had a very crowded cast, most fans

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:52.300
felt as though Levi was a great replacement
for the part, and his dry bravado worked well

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.700
with the Asgardian swordsman.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:59.160
Although Levi's Fandral had a brief and fatal
cameo in Thor: Ragnarok, he had apparently

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:01.120
already reached his wit's end with Marvel.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:05.620
As he told CinemaBlend, he was actually hoping
for his character to be killed off because

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:10.420
Marvel had failed to develop any of the Warriors
Three, and he was apparently grateful that

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:13.040
Cate Blanchett's Hela finished the job in
Ragnarok.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:18.979
In the second season of Amazon's Golden-Globe
winning series The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel , Rachel

00:06:18.979 --> 00:06:23.550
Brosnahan's newly-divorced Midge Maisel vacations
with her family to the Catskills in upstate

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:24.080
New York.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.460
It's here that Midge is set-up with dreamy
doctor Benjamin Ettenberg, played with memorable

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:30.180
swagger by Zachary Levi.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:34.719
Midge and Benjamin have a rocky start, but
eventually their undeniable chemistry gets

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:35.600
the best of both of them.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.710
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,
Levi admitted that although he'd seen the

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:43.900
series' pilot, he actually didn't know that
the show was picked up before he signed on:

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:49.180
"Then I got an offer to join, so my first
bit of homework was bingeing the first season,

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.980
all in essentially a day, and I immediately
wanted to be a part of this.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:57.060
It's so well executed on every level, from
the top down, and to get to share screen time

00:06:57.069 --> 00:07:00.460
with Rachel Brosnahan in that role, that's
an offer you can't refuse."

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.140
"People think if they buy me things I'll work
harder to keep them alive."

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:03.860
"Are they right?

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:04.660
Yes."

